import LOEIS.A265.A265141.Defs

set_option linter.unusedVariables false

/-!
# A265141

Irregular table read by rows: n-th row lists the 9 n-gonal numbers of a 3 X 3 semimagic square with the smallest magic sum. The terms of each row are arranged in the manner shown in A261816.

The 45 terms known to OEIS, indexed from `3`.

Skeleton generated by `lake exe oeis-gen`; every declaration is a `sorry` placeholder.
-/

namespace A265141

/-- Known terms of `flat`, starting at index `3`. -/
def flatData : List flatRetType :=
  [15, 66, 630, 231, 435, 45, 465, 210, 36, 16,
    529, 2704, 1024, 1936, 289, 2209, 784, 256, 651, 54626,
    356972, 135751, 241001, 35497, 275847, 116622, 19780, 6, 39621, 481671,
